-- title:
--   Residual Hecke eigensystems lift to complete discrete valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \geq 1$ (nonzero), an integer weight $k$ with $1 \leq k$, and a set $S$ of natural numbers. Let $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_k(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the linear operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N k`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$. Let $p$ be a prime, $F$ a field of characteristic $p$, and $\theta : \mathbb{T} \to F$ a ring homomorphism. Then there exists a ring $\mathcal{O}'$ which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, such that the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}'$, together with a ring homomorphism $\chi : \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}'$ for which the kernel of $\chi$ followed by the residue map $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}'/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}'}$ equals $\ker \theta$.
--
--   This is the lifting statement for residual Hecke eigensystems in the style of Deligne–Serre: a homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra to a field of characteristic $p$ is, after passing to kernels, the reduction of a characteristic-zero eigensystem valued in a complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field. It is used in the construction of the characteristic-zero Galois representation attached to a mod $p$ Hecke eigensystem, in particular in the analysis of inertia at a prime where a Hecke operator annihilates the eigensystem; the weight hypothesis $k \geq 1$ enters through the finiteness of $\mathbb{T}$ as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeAlgebra_exists_ringHom_ker_residue_comp_eq_ker_of_one_le.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_ker_residue_comp_eq_ker_of_one_le
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (k : ℤ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) (S : Set ℕ) (hint : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N k)
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {F : Type} [Field F] [CharP F p]
    (θ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S →+* F) :
    ∃ (𝒪' : Type) (_ : CommRing 𝒪') (_ : IsDomain 𝒪') (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪')
      (_ : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪') 𝒪')
      (_ : Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪')) (_ : CharZero 𝒪'),
      (p : 𝒪') ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪' ∧
      ∃ χ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S →+* 𝒪',
        RingHom.ker ((IsLocalRing.residue 𝒪').comp χ) = RingHom.ker θ := by sorry
